<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Raja Dahir</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 712</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a> · Also known as Dahir of Sindh</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Raja Dahir was the last <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hinduism">Hindu</a> king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sindh">Sindh</a>, of the Brahman dynasty founded by his father <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tashkent">Chach</a>. Ruling from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aror">Aror</a> in the late 7th and early 8th centuries, he faced the expedition sent by the Umayyad governor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-hajjaj-ibn-yusuf">al-Hajjaj ibn Yusuf</a> after attacks on Arab ships near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/debal">Debal</a>. He was defeated and killed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-ibn-qasim">Muhammad ibn Qasim</a> in 712, and Sindh became part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/umayyad-caliphate">Umayyad Caliphate</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/raja-dahir.jpg" alt="Raja Dahir" width="320" height="356" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mb1010 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:King_Dahir_of_Aror.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
